/T (Austria's deposit return scheme has been running since the first of January 2025, covering single-use PET bottles and aluminium cans between one-tenth of a litre and three litres, each carrying a refundable deposit of twenty-five cents. The system is coordinated by a dedicated non-profit body, with the technical side of tracking containers and processing refunds handled by outside software specialists. Retailers of every size, from small corner shops to large supermarket chains, are obliged to accept empty containers bearing the official deposit logo. Barely a year after the launch, more than eighty percent of all containers placed on the market were already being returned, comfortably ahead of schedule. The Austrian government is now aiming even higher, setting its sights on a ninety percent collection rate by 2027, two years before the EU-wide deadline.)
/E (Austria's deposit return scheme has been running since the first of January 2025, covering single-use PET bottles and aluminium cans between one-tenth of a litre and three litres, each carrying a refundable deposit of twenty-five cents. The system is coordinated by a dedicated non-profit body, with the technical side of tracking containers and processing refunds handled by outside software specialists. Retailers of every size, from small corner shops to large supermarket chains, are obliged to accept empty containers bearing the official deposit logo. Barely a year after the launch, more than eighty percent of all containers placed on the market were already being returned, comfortably ahead of schedule. The Austrian government is now aiming even higher, setting its sights on a ninety percent collection rate by 2027, two years before the EU-wide deadline.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [8]
>>
