/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 109 0 R
/T (Few peaks in the Polish highlands 7.1.______ as much symbolic weight as Giewont. Rising to 1,894 metres above sea level, this iconic massif dominates the skyline above Zakopane and has long captured the imagination of hikers, poets, and patriots 7.2.______. Its distinctive silhouette - said 7.3.______ a sleeping knight - is so deeply embedded in Polish cultural identity that many consider it the unofficial emblem of the Tatra Mountains.)
/E (Few peaks in the Polish highlands 7.1.______ as much symbolic weight as Giewont. Rising to 1,894 metres above sea level, this iconic massif dominates the skyline above Zakopane and has long captured the imagination of hikers, poets, and patriots 7.2.______. Its distinctive silhouette - said 7.3.______ a sleeping knight - is so deeply embedded in Polish cultural identity that many consider it the unofficial emblem of the Tatra Mountains.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
385 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 109 0 R
/T (The ascent, though not technically demanding by alpine standards, should not be underestimated. The final stretch involves steep chains bolted into the rock face, requiring 7.4.______ physical fitness and a level head. The reward, 7.5.______, is considerable: a sweeping panorama stretching from the High Tatras to the foothills of Lesser Poland, and a close-up view of the steel cross erected on the summit in 1901 to mark the turn of the century.)
/E (The ascent, though not technically demanding by alpine standards, should not be underestimated. The final stretch involves steep chains bolted into the rock face, requiring 7.4.______ physical fitness and a level head. The reward, 7.5.______, is considerable: a sweeping panorama stretching from the High Tatras to the foothills of Lesser Poland, and a close-up view of the steel cross erected on the summit in 1901 to mark the turn of the century.)
/Pg 23 0 R
