/Title (Tarde drew an important distinction between two kinds of imitation. The first he called custom: the slow, steady copying of old models, handed down from parents to children, from one generation to the next. Custom changes little and changes slowly. The second he called fashion: the rapid spread of something new, often borrowed from outsiders or from distant, admired groups, cutting across families and traditions. Fashion moves fast precisely because it ignores the boundaries that custom respects.)
/Dest [19 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 2394 0 R
/Prev 2431 0 R
/Next 2474 0 R
