/Title (Few peaks in the Polish highlands 7.1.______ as much symbolic weight as Giewont. Rising to 1,894 metres above sea level, this iconic massif dominates the skyline above Zakopane and has long captured the imagination of hikers, poets, and patriots 7.2.______. Its distinctive silhouette - said 7.3.______ a sleeping knight - is so deeply embedded in Polish cultural identity that many consider it the unofficial emblem of the Tatra Mountains.)
/Dest [23 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 2481 0 R
/Next 2513 0 R
>>
endobj
