/Title (Finally, Tarde made a claim that still unsettles some readers: fashion, if it survives long enough, does not remain fashion forever. It eventually settles down and hardens into a new custom, only to be challenged, one day, by the next wave of imitation. In this way, he suggested, a society is never simply static or simply changing - it is always doing both at once, absorbing the new until it becomes the old.)
/Dest [19 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 2394 0 R
/Prev 2494 0 R
/Next 2517 0 R
>>
