/Title (The ascent, though not technically demanding by alpine standards, should not be underestimated. The final stretch involves steep chains bolted into the rock face, requiring 7.4.______ physical fitness and a level head. The reward, 7.5.______, is considerable: a sweeping panorama stretching from the High Tatras to the foothills of Lesser Poland, and a close-up view of the steel cross erected on the summit in 1901 to mark the turn of the century.)
