/Title (Tarde's theory did not receive immediate recognition in his own country, where rival schools of sociology dominated academic life. Yet decades later, scholars studying the spread of new technologies, popular culture, and even rumours online would return to his work, seeing in his nineteenth-century observations of judges' courtrooms and country towns an early sketch of ideas that would only become fully relevant in the age of mass communication.)
/Dest [19 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 2394 0 R
